## STEP 2 — Ontology Manager: the object type (~15 min)

Create a new object type over the Step-1 dataset:

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Display name | `[SA New Dev] Project Summary` (keep it project-agnostic — non-project rows live here too) |
| API name | `saNewDevProjectSummary` |
| Backing dataset | `sa_new_dev_project_summary` |
| Primary key | `projectSummaryId` |
| **Edit history** | **ON** (powers the history panel) |
| **Action log** | **ON** (powers the Action Log Timeline) |

Properties (map 1:1 from the dataset columns):

| Property | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `projectSummaryId` | string (PK) | **Subject key.** Projects: the real `projectId`. Arbitrary subjects: a slug (`program_cascade_reporting`) |
| `summaryText` | string | the summary itself (markdown) |
| `charLimit` | integer | per-row limit; the save function applies the default (600) on first save |
| `sourceMode` | string | `manual` \| `ai_generated` \| `ai_edited` — manual saves write `manual` |
| `sourceInteractionId` | string, nullable | AI provenance — **null for handwritten rows** |
| `sourceOnePagerHash` | string, nullable | AI provenance — **null for handwritten rows** |
| `lastSavedByUserId` | string | who saved last (passed explicitly — functions can't read the user) |
| `firstSavedAt` | timestamp | set once, on the first save |
| `lastSavedAt` | timestamp | every save |
| `version` | integer | +1 per save |

Then register the **FK link**: ProjectSummary → your project object type, mapping `projectSummaryId` → `projectId`, cardinality one-to-one. No join dataset (FK links never need one). **Subject generality:** for non-project rows the link simply resolves to nothing — Foundry links don't enforce integrity, so this is harmless and intended.

